GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): each top-screen line's fades, for the lighting.

GPU2D_Soft records, per main-engine line, the master brightness and the colour-effect registers
(BLDCNT, EVY) the line was drawn with. The game fades the screen to white or black with them (a
cave's exit flash, a warp's fade); the lighting lights the scene under the fade and applies the
fade again, instead of lighting the faded picture (shapes and shadows showing through a white
screen).

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU2D_Soft.h	2026-11-12 23:53:00.555741739 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU2D_Soft.h	2026-11-12 23:53:00.565896485 -0500
@@ -46,6 +46,12 @@
     u32* WideOwner[2] {};
     // GoldLink (UC11): per main-engine line, where the 3D layer shows: 1 on top, 2 under a
     // 2D layer (opaque or blended), 0 not at all. Column = screen x + MaxSide (the wide sides included).
+    // GoldLink (UC11): per main-engine line, the screen-wide fades the engine applies after
+    // composing (master brightness; the colour effect's brightness on the 3D layer), so the
+    // lighting can light the scene under a fade and put the fade back.
+    u16 LineMasterBright[192] {};
+    u16 LineBlendCnt[192] {};
+    u8 LineEVY[192] {};
     u8 Layer3D[192][256 + 2 * MaxSide] {};
     // The strips' width when drawn.
     int WideDrawn[2] {};
--- a/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp	2026-11-12 23:53:00.555687617 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU2D_Soft.cpp	2026-11-12 23:53:00.565810112 -0500
@@ -116,6 +116,13 @@
     // GoldLink (UC11): this line's 3D mask starts empty; DrawScanline_BGOBJ fills it.
     if (CurUnit->Num == 0 && line < 192)
         memset(Layer3D[line], 0, sizeof(Layer3D[line]));
+    // GoldLink (UC11): this line's fades, as the engine will apply them, for the lighting.
+    if (CurUnit->Num == 0 && line < 192)
+    {
+        LineMasterBright[line] = CurUnit->MasterBrightness;
+        LineBlendCnt[line] = CurUnit->BlendCnt;
+        LineEVY[line] = CurUnit->EVY;
+    }
 
     if (CurUnit->Num == 0)
